71879839897,-0.11788645386695862,-3.2186455882765586e-06,-4.768370445162873e-07,-2.3245540432981215e-05,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-0.00018821375851985067,-3.576278118089249e-07,-4.458328112377785e-05,-0.1637624055147171,-3.576278118089249e-07,-0.006489986553788185,-0.0001006075763143599,-0.05423132702708244,-0.00014661667228210717,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-0.8497815728187561,-0.04773552715778351,-0.10778095573186874,-1.0728830375228426e-06,0.0,-0.265215665102005,-8.22540732769994e-06,-0.3997546136379242,-1.7077579498291016,-1.1920928244535389e-07,0.0,-1.1920922133867862e-06,0.0,-0.09847366809844971,-0.5062499046325684,-0.0004677870310842991,-2.861018856492592e-06,-7.152555099310121e-07,-9.179073458653875e-06,-2.3841855067985307e-07,-0.0008747326792217791,-2.50339189733495e-06,0.0,-9.536738616588991e-07,-0.001508409040980041,-0.0006055190460756421,0.0,0.0,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-0.001587560516782105,-1.7404405298293568e-05,-2.7418097943154862e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,10061,400,64,4779,400,65,4779,400,66,4779,323,400,67,3,387,6785,1931,5109,1741,429,400,18,21,64,488,220,19,65,488,220,19,66,488,220,18,67,284,220,17,20,2418,220,7379,279,7192,897,315,198,78045,64,1124,15136,1124,26888,90,65,92,1124,15136,1124,26888,58,18,15370,66,92,1124,15136,1124,26888,58,19,15370,67,92,7110,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nLet $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ and $d$ be positive real numbers such that $36a + 4b + 4c + 3d = 25.$  Find the maximum value of\n\\[a \\times \\sqrt{b} \\times \\sqrt[3]{c} \\times \\sqrt[4]{d}.\\]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"2de17349d2d1c86b044b03c314cdb17fa7aaf2bf8b169f36bc351ecf136830e7"},"seconds":89.52051973342896,"seed":299041771582075571,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the maximum value of the expression \\(a \\times \\sqrt{b} \\times \\sqrt[3]{c} \\times \\sqrt[4]{d}\\) under the constraint \\(36a + 4b + 4c + 3d = 25\\), we use the method of Lagrange multipliers or apply the AM-GM inequality for simplicity.\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the expression and the constraint for clarity:\n\\[ f(a, b, c, d) = a \\cdot \\sqrt{b} \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{c} \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{d} \\]\nsubject to\n\\[ 36a + 4b + 4c + 3d = 25. \\]\n\nWe apply the AM-GM inequality to the terms in the constraint. The AM-GM inequality states that for non-negative real numbers \\(x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n\\),\n\\[ \\frac{x_1 + x_2 + \\cdots + x_n}{n} \\geq \\sqrt[n]{x_1 x_2 \\cdots x_n}, \\]\nwith equality if and only if \\(x_1 = x_2 = \\cdots = x_n\\).\n\nWe apply AM-GM to the terms \\(36a, 4b, 4c, 3d\\):\n\\[ \\frac{36a + 4b + 4c + 3d}{4} \\geq \\sqrt[4]{36a \\cdot 4b \\cdot 4c \\cdot 3d}. \\]\nGiven the constraint \\(36a + 4b + 4c + 3d = 25\\), we have:\n\\[ \\frac{25}{4} \\geq \\sqrt[4]{36a \\cdot 4b \\cdot 4c \\cdot 3d}. \\]\nRaising both sides to the fourth power, we get:\n\\[ \\left( \\frac{25}{4} \\right)^4 \\geq 36a \\cdot 4b \\cdot 4c \\cdot 3d. \\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[ \\left( \\frac{25}{4} \\right)^4 = \\frac{390625}{256}. \\]\nThus,\n\\[ \\frac{390625}{256} \\geq 144abcd. \\]\nSolving for \\(abcd\\), we get:\n\\[ abcd \\leq \\frac{390625}{256 \\cdot 144} = \\frac{390625}{36864} = \\frac{390625}{36864} = \\frac{390625}{36864} = \\frac{125}{1152}. \\]\n\nTo achieve equality in the AM-GM inequality, we need:\n\\[ 36a = 4b = 4c = 3d. \\]\nLet \\(36a = 4b = 4c = 3d = k\\). Then,\n\\[ a = \\frac{k}{36}, \\quad b = \\frac{k}{4}, \\quad c = \\frac{k}{4}, \\quad d = \\frac{k}{3}. \\]\nSubstituting these into the constraint, we get:\n\\[ k + k + k + k = 25 \\implies 4k = 25 \\implies k = \\frac{25}{4}. \\]\nThus,\n\\[ a = \\frac{25}{4 \\cdot 36} = \\frac{25}{144}, \\quad b = \\frac{25}{4 \\cdot 4} = \\frac{25}{16}, \\quad c = \\frac{25}{4 \\cdot 4} = \\frac{25}{16}, \\quad d = \\frac{25}{4 \\cdot 3} = \\frac{25}{12}. \\]\nThe expression we want to maximize is:\n\\[ a \\cdot \\sqrt{b} \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{c} \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{d} = \\frac{25}{144} \\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{25}{16}} \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{25}{16}} \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{\\frac{25}{12}} = \\frac{25}{144} \\cdot \\frac{5}{4} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt[3]{25}}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt[4]{25}}{\\sqrt[4]{12}}. \\]\nSimplifying, we get:\n\\[ \\frac{25}{144} \\cdot \\frac{5}{4} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt[3]{25}}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt[4]{25}}{\\sqrt[4]{12}} = \\frac{25 \\cdot 5 \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{25} \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{25}}{144 \\cdot 4 \\cdot 2 \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{12}} = \\frac{125 \\cdot \\sqrt[12]{25^4 \\cdot 25^3 \\cdot 25}}{1152 \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{12}} = \\frac{125 \\cdot \\sqrt[12]{25^8}}{1152 \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{12}} = \\frac{125 \\cdot 25^{2/3}}{1152 \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{12}} = \\frac{125 \\cdot 5^{4/3}}{1152 \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{12}} = \\frac{125 \\cdot 5^{4/3}}{1152 \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{12}} = \\frac{125 \\cdot 5^{4/3}}{1152 \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{12}} = \\frac{125}{1152}. \\]\n\nTherefore, the maximum value is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{125}{1152}}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{125}{1152}}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
